Here is the core issue: In JavaScript, calling a function synchronously (like `setInterval`) inside a function that might already be executing (like your game loop) can cause erratic timing behavior, including freezing.

The solution is to move `score++` out of the `forEach` loop. These two tasks are completely unrelated—if you increment the score every single frame, you’d rapidly trigger this event multiple times per frame, causing a performance stall. Instead of checking for collisions 30-60+ times per second and immediately scoring on each, do both in a single pass.

